<title>USA: Great Western sets June 13 merger vote.</title>
<headline>Great Western sets June 13 merger vote.</headline>
<dateline>CHATSWORTH, Calif. 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Great Western Financial Corp said Tuesday it has set June 13 for a special meeting of stockholders to vote on its proposed merger with Washington Mutual Inc.</p>
<p>It said May 9 will be the record date for the special meeting, scheduled for 1000 PDT/1700 GMT at the Great Western Employee Center in Chatsworth.</p>
<p>Great Western noted it has retained Goldman, Sachs &amp; Co and Merrill Lynch &amp; Co to act as its financial advisors in connection with the merger, as well as the competing merger proposal by H.F. Ahmanson &amp; Co.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610.))</p>
